UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<div class="accordion__content" id="Why_study_this_degree-1" style="--panel-height: 334px;"> <p>If you are a practising Registered nurse with a desire to improve your clinical knowledge this program is for you. This partnership program is a unique collaboration between The University of Notre Dame Australia and several leading health providers.</p><p>The program is only available to students who have a nursing degree and are registered with the Nursing and Midwifery Board of Australia and have a graduate employee contract with the partnering health providers. Upon completion, you will have the skills and knowledge to apply your expertise in the clinical area.</p><p>You will complete units in advanced health assessment, clinical nursing practice and nursing governance. As part of the program, you undertake a series of clinical rotations and written projects.</p><p>Upon graduation, you can embark on a further year of study leading to a Graduate Diploma of Clinical Nursing and, later, a Master of Nursing.</p> </div>',
    total_course_duration = '0.5 years full-time or equivalent part-time',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<div class="accordion__content" id="Entry_requirements-3" style="--panel-height: 543px;"> <p>There are two distinct entry pathways for students into this award program. According to the MOU industry students will enrol into Pathway A or B:</p><ul><li>Pathway A - Via an existing partnership between Notre Dame and an external healthcare provider to support the Graduate programs.</li><li>Pathway B - Direct entry, full fee paying, OR existing partnership new graduate student employed in an approved healthcare setting.</li></ul><p>To be eligible for admission to the Graduate Certificate in Clinical Nursing applicants must also meet the following specific requirements:</p><ul><li>Current license to practice as a Registered Nurse with the Nursing and Midwifery Board of Australia or provisional registration; whichever is applicable at the time of commencement.</li><li>Nursing or other appropriate degree or the equivalent</li><li>Candidates must be employed in a graduate position with a participating health service provider and have their hospital''''s support to undertake the program.</li></ul><p>Please note:</p><ul><li>Interviews for the Graduate Certificate in Clinical Nursing will be at the discretion of the health service and conducted on site.</li><li>Please be aware that the standard course costs do not apply for this program. Course costs are reduced due to the unique nature of this hospital-based, university-supported learning program.</li></ul> </div>',
    apply_form = 'https://und-search.funnelback.squiz.cloud/s/redirect?collection=und~sp-program&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.notredame.edu.au%2Fprograms%2Fschool-of-nursing%2Fpostgraduate%2Fgraduate-certificate-in-clinical-nursing&auth=ZO6u7Eevs7rfDlH477f%2ByQ&profile=programs&rank=142&query=%21FunDoesNotExist%3Apadrenull',
    created_at = '2026-06-26 23:37:52',
    updated_at = '2026-06-26 23:37:52'
WHERE cricos_course_code = 'UNKNOWN';


